---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

const lastUpdated = '20 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of Use for the PS Laser production management application."
  path="/terms"
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of Use" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="last-updated reveal">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>1. Who these terms apply to</h2>
        <p>
          PS Laser is an internal manufacturing operations application, made available to
          employees and authorized staff of PS Laser and companies PS Laser is contracted to
          serve. By signing in with a PIN and account issued to you, you agree to these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What the app does</h2>
        <p>
          PS Laser provides order intake, production workflow tracking (Laser Cutting,
          Punching, Powder Coating), machine and worker allocation, delivery supervision,
          reporting, and an in-app AI assistant that answers operational questions using your
          company's own live data. Functionality is described accurately at the time of
          publishing and may change as the app is developed further.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Accounts and access</h2>
        <p>
          Accounts are created through in-app registration and require approval from an Owner
          or Manager before use (the first account registered for a company becomes its Owner
          account automatically). You are responsible for keeping your PIN confidential and for
          activity that occurs under your account. A Worker account's access is intentionally
          limited to their own assigned machine queue and jobs; other roles have broader access
          appropriate to their responsibilities.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the app only for legitimate business operations related to your role.</li>
          <li>Do not attempt to access data or functionality outside what your role is granted.</li>
          <li>Do not attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or reverse-engineer the app or its backend services.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Data handling</h2>
        <p>
          How we collect, use, and store data is described in full in our
          <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>, which is incorporated into these terms by
          reference.
        </p>

        <h2>6. No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The app is provided on an "as is" basis. We do not guarantee uninterrupted
          availability, and we make no claims about specific response times or uptime beyond
          what is separately and explicitly agreed with your company.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms as the app changes. Material changes will be reflected in
          the "last updated" date above.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:pslaser24@gmail.com">pslaser24@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vh, 64px) 0;
  }
</style>
